      "description": "Nvidia is opening an investigation into reports that CEO Jensen Huang was the \"target of a foreign intelligence effort,\" the company's board of directors said Sunday.\nThe announcement came after Huang acknowledged to the board that he had been intimate with a business executive whom US intelligence determined was gathering information for Beijing, The New York Times reported.\nHuang apologised in a message to the company, according to the Times. \"I was unfaithful to my wife,\" he said. \"My actions hurt her and our children. There is no excuse for what I did. I am deeply sorry.\"\nNvidia's board said in a statement it has \"no reason to believe that either national security or Nvidia secrets were compromised,\" but that its inquiry would examine all available information. Huang \"fully supports the review and has committed to cooperating with it,\" the board said.\nHuang, 63, will remain CEO during the investigation.\nThe Times reported last month that US intelligence agencies had discovered",
